+/*
+ * Audio description of the campaign's cutscenes: what is seen, said as a
+ * shot starts, or as long into it as what it says takes to happen, and
+ * held while a character is speaking: said in the gap after. In the cutscene
+ * maps each is keyed to the shot's number, counting from one as each
+ * camera starts (the game plays them in the same order every time, and
+ * the same camera is used again for another moment). In a mission, which
+ * a saved game may be loaded into part way, to the camera's name. A shot
+ * with nothing new to see - the same faces, talking - has no line.
+ *
+ * Written by watching each cutscene; eta_cameraShots 1 takes the
+ * pictures they were written from. Each line is timed against the
+ * cutscene's recorded dialogue (the scripts play it the same every time)
+ * to start when what it describes is seen and to end before the next
+ * character speaks, so most are short, and a shot whose talking leaves
+ * no gap goes undescribed rather than talked over.
+ */
